<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield falls to 12.29 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield falls to 12.29 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of three-month MKM discount Treasury bills fell to 12.29 percent at an auction on Tuesday from 14.59 percent at the last auction on May 20, the National Bank said.</p>
<p>Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   May 27	     May 20</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ43K2808972     KZ43K2108977</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  700		  650</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, million tenge)	 1,869		2,610</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	 700		  672</p>
<p> Average price			 97.02 pct	  96.48</p>
<p> Average yield			 12.29		14.59</p>
<p> Tenor				   91 days	    91 days</p>
<p> Maturity				Aug 28, 1997     Aug 21, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
